$x = random(1, 10, 1);
$y = $x + 2010;
Context("Percent");
$p = Percent((0.0042*$x**3 - 0.0529*$x**2 + 0.0212*$x + 32.842)/100);

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
The percentage of births in the U.S. delivered via cesarean section in a year can be given by the formula [`p = 0.0042x^3-0.0529x^2+0.0212x+32.842`] where [`x`] is the number of years since 2010.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
What percent of births in the US in the year [$y] were cesarean deliveries?

[_]{$p}{10}

END_PGML

